  "body": {
    "id": "lem:optimized-mixture-envelope",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Every experiment in the target class satisfies the optimized observed-law total-variation lower envelope\n\\[\n \\mathfrak L_\\alpha^\\star\n \\ge\n \\sup_{0\\le\\eta<1-2\\alpha}\n (1-2\\alpha-\\eta)\\Omega_{\\mathcal D,\\Gamma}(\\eta).\n\\]\nIn particular, for \\(\\eta_\\alpha=(1-2\\alpha)/2\\),\n\\[\n \\mathfrak L_\\alpha^\\star\n \\ge \\eta_\\alpha\\Omega_{\\mathcal D,\\Gamma}(\\eta_\\alpha).\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "alpha",
      "L_star",
      "Omega_D_gamma",
      "D_design",
      "Gamma",
      "eta_alpha"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:honest-minimax-length",
      "lem:mixture-modulus-length-lower-bound"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(0\\le\\eta<1-2\\alpha\\).  For every \\(K\\in\\mathcal C_\\alpha\\), Lemma \\(\\mathrm{lem:mixture\\text{-}modulus\\text{-}length\\text{-}lower\\text{-}bound}\\) gives\n\\[\n \\sup_{Y\\in\\mathcal Y_{M,\\Gamma}}\n \\mathbb E^K_{\\mathcal D,Y}[\\operatorname{len}(I_K)]\n \\ge\n (1-2\\alpha-\\eta)\\Omega_{\\mathcal D,\\Gamma}(\\eta).\n\\]\nThe right-hand side depends on the experiment and \\(\\eta\\), but not on \\(K\\).  Taking the infimum over \\(K\\in\\mathcal C_\\alpha\\) and using Definition \\(\\mathrm{def:honest\\text{-}minimax\\text{-}length}\\) therefore yields\n\\[\n \\mathfrak L_\\alpha^\\star\n \\ge\n (1-2\\alpha-\\eta)\\Omega_{\\mathcal D,\\Gamma}(\\eta).\n\\]\nThis inequality holds for every \\(\\eta\\) in the displayed nonempty range; hence taking the supremum over \\(\\eta\\) proves the first claim.  Assumption \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1/2)\\) gives\n\\[\n 0<\\eta_\\alpha=\\frac{1-2\\alpha}{2}<1-2\\alpha,\n \\qquad\n 1-2\\alpha-\\eta_\\alpha=\\eta_\\alpha.\n\\]\nSubstitution of this admissible value in the pointwise inequality proves the convenient corollary.",
    "justification": "This takes the pointwise all-kernel testing inequality over every admissible total-variation radius, rather than fixing one convenient radius.",
    "gap": "It is an observed-law total-variation lower envelope; it does not compare the modulus with the predictable-AIPW radius.",
    "consumer": "The adaptive minimax sandwich uses this optimized lower side and retains the fixed-radius display as a corollary.",
